dArkOS: START ON SYSTEM > LAST PLAYED SYSTEM.
UI Settings > START ON SYSTEM could start ES on one fixed system only. The new
choice, LAST PLAYED SYSTEM ("lastsystem"), starts it on the system a game was
last started from, with the cursor on that game in its list; with "start on
game list" or the system view hidden it opens that list.
- launch() saves the system whose list the game is started from (a collection
  or a group, as the user browsed it) and the game's path to es_settings.cfg
  (LastSystem, LastGame) at once: the console is often switched off without
  quitting ES. Only while LAST PLAYED SYSTEM is chosen.
- goToStart() finds the system (a group's member stands for its group), puts
  the list's cursor on the game, found by its path (a collection's entry has its
  game's path), and goes there. With nothing saved yet, or the system gone or
  hidden, ES starts as with NONE.
- It is the default. es_settings.cfg keeps only what differs from the default,
  so a user who had NONE (never written) gets it, after an update as well; a
  system chosen by name stays, and NONE chosen now is written as "".

